# webkit-egl-blob-cache-env.patch: keep the GPU driver's compiled shaders on
# disk (EGL_ANDROID_blob_cache).
#
# Android GPU drivers (Adreno, Mali) do not persist compiled shaders or program
# binaries themselves. They hand each one to the application through
# EGL_ANDROID_blob_cache and ask for it back the next time; Android's EGL
# wrapper backs that with a file per app. Under libhybris nobody registers the
# callbacks, so every WebProcess compiles every shader from source again —
# during the first scrolls of every new page process, on the compositor thread.
#
# WEBKIT_EGL_BLOB_CACHE_DIR=<dir> (unset = off = upstream): GLDisplay registers
# get/set callbacks backed by <dir>/egl-blob-cache.bin, shared by all engine
# processes (flock, append-only records, loaded once per process, 32 MB cap,
# a torn tail is trimmed on load). Nothing happens if the display does not
# advertise the extension. The entry point is looked up with
# eglGetProcAddress(), not libepoxy, whose stub aborts when a symbol is
# missing. WEBKIT_EGL_BLOB_CACHE_LOG=1 logs load/store/miss.
#
# The directory must be writable inside the sandbox and private to the app.
# Verify on device with the log: second launch should show "N blobs" > 0 and
# no "store" lines on a page already visited.
#
# ---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLDisplay.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLDisplay.cpp
